# Delivery

- Read `docs/ROADMAP.md`, `docs/DELIVERY_WORKFLOW.md`, `docs/CONSUMER_REQUESTS.md`, and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before adding public API.
- “What’s next?” starts discovery. Prefer a filled file in `docs/requests/` over speculation. It does not authorize a component catalog dump. Do not wait for a chat paste.
- Implement one lane per change: `tokens`, `react`, or `react-native`. Shared token work may land first when both renderers need it.
- Do not add a new public component, utility family, or renderer without an accepted plan and a filled `docs/requests/<consumer>-<surface>.md`.
- One consumer is enough to request and ship a primitive. Prefer reusing an existing surface over adding a parallel one.
- Public names are generic and reusable. Domain copy stays in the requesting product.
- Treat the accepted plan as scope. Stop and discuss material API expansion.
- Apply `docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md`. New public web surfaces get a gallery catalog section in the same change. Record remaining work if unfinished.
